literate-ai is a software-neutral lifecycle framework for spec-led AI
development. Its command line harness, litai, drives specification, planning,
generation, build, test, verification, locking and release of a project as
reviewed, evidence-gated steps, and can delegate native work to the build
system a project already uses (make, CMake, Bazel and others).

Daemonarchy installs /usr/src and /usr/ports on every system; litai is the
harness through which source and ports operations are meant to be run. The
litai-mcp program exposes the same harness over the Model Context Protocol.
